1. Reading and changing. You may read the Enterprise code, copy it for your own study, and
   change it, for example to fix a problem or try an idea, on your own systems.

2. Using it in production. You may run the Enterprise code, changed or not, to monitor
   systems you or your organisation operate only while you hold a valid WatchLog Enterprise
   licence key for that installation, and only within what the key allows (its features,
   its units and its end date). Without a valid key, the Enterprise code stays switched off,
   and you may not change it or WatchLog so that it runs anyway.

3. Development and testing. You may run the Enterprise code without a key to develop and
   test changes, in environments that do not monitor production systems.

4. No redistribution. You may not sell, rent, sublicense, publish, host for others or
   otherwise pass on the Enterprise code or your changes to it, on their own or as part of
